This PR introduces a new Twig tag `{% add %}`, that works like this:

```twig
{% add to body %}
  <div>I will appear at the end of the body</div>
{% endadd %}

{% add to head %}
  {# Add an additional head tag #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="my-fancy-style.css">
{% endadd %}
```

Currently the content inside the tag will be rendered and simply put into `$GLOBALS['TL_HEAD']` and `$GLOBALS['TL_BODY']` but the idea is to use the response context in the future as soon it supports these things. :slightly_smiling_face:.

Optionally, you can define an identifier to make sure the content gets output only once when used multiple times - this will basically use a key in the above global arrays:

```twig
{% for i in range(0, 10) %}
  {% add 'foo' to body %}
    <script type="application/javascript">
      console.log('I will only be executed once!');
    </script>
  {% endadd %}
{% endfor %}
```

This feature for instance allows to easily add small inline scripts that are then output only once - e.g. for displaying a splash screen, scrolling the viewport, and so on. In #4444 I already stumbled about multiple of these scenarios.

## Description
By default we need to support CAE feature by enabling the custom policy for [CAE ](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/conditional-access/concept-continuous-access-evaluation) feature. However we have bugs about the conditions and parameters so we plan to fix in this pr.

Simply speaking the policy will be enabled with below conditions:
- If the User doesn't set any option, the policy will be set
- If the User sets the options, but if pipeline is null, the policy will be set
- If the Pipeline is set, but there are no policies, the policy will be set.
- If the Pipeline has policy, but not the bearer token authentication policy, then the new policy will be set.

And regarding the parameter we need to call [core func](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/blob/main/sdk/core/core-rest-pipeline/src/policies/bearerTokenAuthenticationPolicy.ts#L136) to construct the policy:

```typescript
 this.pipeline.addPolicy(
      coreRestPipeline.bearerTokenAuthenticationPolicy({
        credential: credentials,
        scopes: `${optionsWithDefaults.credentialScopes}`, // TODO: need to confirm the scope is correct!!!
        challengeCallbacks: {
          authorizeRequestOnChallenge:
            coreClient.authorizeRequestOnClaimChallenge
        }
      })
    );
```

