## Design overview
There are 3 main functions to this service: `sendToken`, `sendNative` and `withdrawNative`. Each of the functions are expecting the funds to be already transferred to a specific deposit address which is generated with following functions:
`depositAddressForSendToken`, `depositAddressForSendNative`, `depositAddressForWithdrawNative`. 

Here is a more detailed overview of the parameters they take:
```
    function depositAddressForSendToken(
        bytes32 nonce,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string calldata destinationAddress,
        string calldata tokenSymbol
    ) external view returns (address);

    function sendToken(
        bytes32 nonce,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string calldata destinationAddress,
        string calldata tokenSymbol
    ) external;
```

```
    function depositAddressForSendNative(
        bytes32 nonce,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string calldata destinationAddress
    ) external view returns (address);

    function sendNative(
        bytes32 nonce,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string calldata destinationAddress
    ) external;
```

```
    function depositAddressForWithdrawNative(bytes32 nonce, address recipient) 
        external view returns (address);

    function withdrawNative(bytes32 nonce, address payable recipient) external;
```
